Date: Wed, 24 Mar 93 01:20:21 EST
From: Brian.Hawthorne@East.Sun.COM (Brian Holt Hawthorne - SunSelect Engineering)
Subject: HEX: Introducing the Hawthorne Exchange

The Hawthorne Exchange - HEx 			(intro, 19 March 1993)

	    Introductory Information and Overview

What is the Hawthorne Exchange?

    HEx is modeled on existing stock and commodity exchanges. However,
    rather than trading in shares of corporations or goods, it trades
    in reputations.

    Any individual can register a reputation on the exchange, and then
    offer shares for sale. This will also give you an investment
    account with HEx, which you can use for buying and selling shares
    on the exchange. If you register additional reputations (for
    example, if have multiple identities on the list), they
    will be tied to your existing account.

    HEx will initially be available only to subscribers of the Extropian
    mailing list.

What good is it?

    HEx was created as an alternative to the zero-sum central banking
    scheme being proposed by others. It will allow creation of
    reputation wealth as individuals improve their reputations through
    better postings.  Conversely, if the quality on the list
    deteriorates, it will also accurately reflect this. If we have
    nothing but flying yogi discussions, look for a market crash.

    If you are curious about what other people think of you, register
    your reputation with HEx and issue some shares. You can measure
    the value of your reputation as a function of share price and total
    outstanding shares.

    If you like what someone is posting, buy shares of their reputation.
    If you don't like what someone is posting, sell their shares.

What units are used for measuring share value?

    The basic unit of value is the Thorne (currency symbol p, Latin1 
    character 240. If your mail software loses the eighth bit, you
    will probably see this as a lower-case 'p').

    The Thorne is indivisible, thus all share prices are in integral
    numbers of Thornes. The Thorne is currently convertible only by buying
    shares on the exchange.

Where does the initial currency come from?

    The Hawthorne Exchange is investing its reputation capital in this
    venture. As the issuer of the currency, they have set the size of
    the money supply at p1,000,000, all of which is currently in the
    hands of the Exchange. They have also issued 10,000 shares in their
    reputation (trading symbol HEX) at an offering price of p100.

    Anyone registering their first reputation with HEx will receive in
    return 100 shares of HEX. HEx has a standing buy order on the
    exchange at the offering price. If nobody else will buy HEX shares
    from you, HEx will. This effectively gives you at least p10,000 of
    starting capital (more if the price of HEx goes up, less if you
    choose to hold on to some of the HEX shares).

What information is public? What is private?

    All reputation names, their current share price, and number of issued
    shares are public information. 

    There will be a daily posting of all reputations, their latest
    price per share, and total number of shares outstanding. All
    postings from HEx will use the prefix HEX:.

    All account information, including balances and share transactions,
    is private between HEx and the account holder. 

    There is currently no support for encryption, but this may
    be added in the future.

How do I use HEx?

    All transactions with HEx are done via email to an automatic server.
    The command is specified in the Subject line. The message body is
    ignored unless otherwise noted.

    Basically, once you have an account, when you are reading Extropians
    and think to yourself, "Gee, that Perry is consistently posting
    great things!", then buy some shares of his reputation (assuming
    he has registered on the exchange. Conversely, if someone starts
    writing inanities, sell some shares of them that you own.

    For detailed information on trading practices and rules, send email
    to 'HEx@sea.east.sun.com' with the Subject: line 'TRADING'.

    For detailed information on the commands available, send email
    to 'HEx@sea.east.sun.com' with the Subject: line 'COMMANDS'.

When will HEx be available?

    Reputation registration and account creation is available today.
    Share offerings and general trading will start in the near future.
    [ Estimated opening date is 1 April 1993. ]

What about other services in the future?

    Investment accounts will be able to be opened without 
    registering a reputation.

    Inter-account transfers of either cash (p) or shares may be
    allowed in the future. This could make individual accounts 
    without reputations a meaningful feature.

    Independant brokerage.

    Conversion to other currencies.

    Encryption.

